Verification (2026-06-10): running `basil rules.txt -v -bc` in
gram/rules/ reproduces all four checked-in generated files
BYTE-IDENTICALLY (1191 states, 0 conflicts).  See test/run_gate.sh.

Runs on x86-64 Linux via ia32 emulation (standard kernels).  basilsim
is the companion parser simulator (same distribution, see README.TXT).

The modern basilcc on GitHub (github.com/mjspncr/basilcc) is a 2016
rewrite serving lzz3: different CLI, different rule syntax, runtime FSM
output — it CANNOT regenerate these tables.
